# secretscan path allowances — root-relative globs.
# tests/fixtures/probes/ holds transcripts captured from loopback stub servers
# with self-signed certificates for synthetic example.test names
# (CONTRIBUTING § Capturing a fixture from a local stub). Their certificates,
# session ids and key shares are high-entropy by nature and protect nothing.
tests/fixtures/probes/*.txt

# Three test modules whose synthetic values read as high-entropy: a test DKIM
# public key (test_dnsevidence.py), the Entra audit CSV's long column names
# (test_reader_entra_audit.py) and example RVTools export file names
# (test_reader_rvtools.py). A line marker would push each line past the
# 110-column lint limit. Tests hold synthetic data only (CONTRIBUTING), and the
# local guard check still scans these files for identifiers.
tests/test_dnsevidence.py
tests/test_reader_entra_audit.py
tests/test_reader_rvtools.py
